  "description": "Fixback for Serilog: WriteTo.Fixback() files the errors your app logs through Serilog into the same Fixback queue as your frontend — an exception as a handled error, a log line as a message grouped by its template, a faulted BackgroundService as unhandled — and records lower levels as breadcrumbs on the error's Trace. Works beside Fixback.AspNetCore's UseFixback() (request context, Correlation id), filing nothing twice.",
